.TH QFW_SUPERMARQ.SH 1 "August 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw Examples"
.SH NAME
qfw_supermarq.sh \- run a SuperMarQ workload through QFw admission control
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
cd "${QFW_SHARE_DIR}/examples"
\&./qfw_supermarq.sh [common-options] run iterations start-qubits \e
  shots increase method backend
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qfw_supermarq.sh
runs a SuperMarQ GHZ or VQE workload through the QFw Slurm-style reservation
driver. It reserves the requested circuit count, qubits, and shots before
launching the application. The reservation is released when the test ends.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I run
Use
.B sync
for synchronous QPM calls or
.B async
for asynchronous submission and completion reads.
.TP
.I iterations
Positive workload iteration count.
.TP
.I start-qubits
Initial circuit width.
.TP
.I shots
Shots per circuit.
.TP
.I increase
Boolean value. When true, each iteration adds one qubit.
.TP
.I method
Use
.B ghz
or
.BR vqe .
.TP
.I backend
QPM provider name. An explicit
.B --backend
option takes precedence.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --service-mode " mode"
Use application-owned
.B local
services or an existing
.B site
QPM.
.TP
.BI --backend " name"
Override the positional backend.
.TP
.BI --site-config " path"
Override the activated site configuration.
.TP
.BI --runtime-config " path"
Override the installed runtime selected by the service mode.
.TP
.B --verbose
Enable shell tracing.
.PP
Common options must precede the positional arguments.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QFW_SUPERMARQ_RESERVATION_COUNT
Override the reserved quantum-task count. It defaults to the iteration count.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run one four-qubit GHZ circuit with 128 shots on NWQSim:
.EX
cd "${QFW_SHARE_DIR}/examples"
\&./qfw_supermarq.sh --service-mode local --backend nwqsim \e
  sync 1 4 128 false ghz nwqsim
.EE
.PP
Run one bounded two-qubit GHZ circuit on a site-owned IQM QPM:
.EX
cd "${QFW_SHARE_DIR}/examples"
\&./qfw_supermarq.sh --service-mode site --backend iqm \e
  sync 1 2 16 false ghz iqm
.EE
